KEY                                TYPE    DEFAULT                  BOUNDS         APPLIES               WHAT
cpu                                int     10                       1 to 10        "fev restart"         The most CPU cores the VM can use
memory_mib                         int     8192                     1024 to 32768  "fev restart"         The most memory the VM can use, in MiB. Memory it isn't using goes back to your Mac
docker.set_context                 bool    true                                    at once               Create the fev Docker context and select it, so docker commands use Fevom
data_allow_backup                  bool    false                                   at once               Include Fevom's data in Time Machine backups. It is one large disk image, which can make backups much larger
network.publish_lan                bool    true                                    at once               Let other devices on your network reach published ports. Ports published on 127.0.0.1 or ::1 stay on this Mac
files.share                        bool    true                                    "fev restart"         Share your Mac's files with the VM, so containers can bind-mount Mac folders
power.pause_in_sleep               bool    true                                    at once               Pause the VM while your Mac sleeps. Containers and machines carry on where they were when it wakes
start_at_login                     bool    false                                   at once               Start Fevom in the background when you log in. The VM starts only when something needs it
network.host_loopback              bool    true                                    at once               Let containers reach servers on your Mac's localhost at host.docker.internal
machines.forward_ports             bool    true                                    at once               Forward the ports machines listen on to localhost on your Mac
machines.expose_ports_to_lan       bool    true                                    at once               Let other devices on your network reach machines' ports that listen on all addresses (0.0.0.0 or ::)
ssh.port                           int     32122                    1 to 65535     at once               The port of Fevom's SSH server, used by ssh fev
ssh.expose_port                    bool    false                                   at once               Let other devices on your network reach Fevom's SSH server. When off, only this Mac can connect
network.subnet                     string  198.19.0.0/16                           "fev restart"         The IPv4 /16 Fevom takes its addresses from, chosen at the first start away from your Mac's networks. Changing it renumbers every container and machine
network.subnet6                    string                                          "fev restart"         The IPv6 /48 (a unique local range) Fevom takes its addresses from, made at the first start
network.direct_access              bool    true                                    at once               Reach containers and machines at their IP addresses from your Mac. Needs the admin helper (sudo fev setup --admin)
network.https                      bool    true                                    at once               Serve fev.local names over HTTPS, with certificates from Fevom's own root certificate, which your Mac trusts after fev setup --https
network.proxy                      string  auto                                    at once               The proxy for image pulls and for containers' and machines' connections: auto follows your Mac's settings, none uses no proxy, or enter a proxy URL
network.proxy_exclude              list    []                                      at once               Hosts, domains and IP ranges (CIDR) reached without the proxy, in addition to your Mac's own exceptions
network.proxy.transparent          bool    true                                    at once               Send containers' and machines' TCP connections through the proxy, without proxy settings inside them
admin.enabled                      bool    true                                    at once               Use the admin helper for direct IP access, fev.local names on your Mac and ports below 1024. Install it with sudo fev setup --admin
files.view_hidden                  bool    false                                   at once               Hide ~/Fevom from Finder's sidebar and the desktop. The folder stays at ~/Fevom
emulation.x86                      bool    true                                    "fev restart docker"  Run x86 Linux software (linux/amd64 images, amd64 machines and 32-bit programs) through translation in the VM
emulation.engine                   string  fex                                     "fev restart"         The x86-64 translator: auto uses Rosetta, and FEX for software known to fail under Rosetta; fex or rosetta forces one. 32-bit programs always use FEX. A machine's emulation setting or a container's dev.fevom.emulation label overrides it
docker.enabled                     bool    true                                    at once               Run the Docker engine. When off, docker commands are refused and Linux machines keep running
docker.node_name                   string  fev                                     "fev restart"         The Docker engine's host name, shown by docker info and to a swarm's nodes
debug.cache_url                    string  https://cache.nixos.org                 at once               The binary cache the Debug Shell's tools are downloaded from. A mirror must serve the cache's own signatures. Applies at the next download
debug.index_url                    string                                          at once               Where the Debug Shell's command index is downloaded from. Empty uses the index that ships with Fevom. Applies at the next download
kubernetes.enabled                 bool    false                                   at once               Run a single-node Kubernetes cluster beside Docker that can run your Docker images. The first start downloads about 250 MB. While on, it uses about a tenth of a CPU core and up to 2 GiB of memory
kubernetes.expose_services_to_lan  bool    false                                   at once               Let other devices on your network reach the cluster's NodePort services. When off, only this Mac can
kubernetes.kubelet                 object  {}                                      at once               Fields of the cluster's kubelet configuration (KubeletConfiguration) as a JSON object. Applying it restarts k3s; workloads keep running
kubernetes.metrics_server          bool    false                                   at once               Run metrics-server in the cluster, for kubectl top
kubernetes.images_url              string                                          at once               Where the cluster's image archive is downloaded from at the first start. Empty uses k3s's release. Its SHA-256 is checked either way
